{{block center|<math>+\frac{b^2\mu}{2}\cos f-\frac{b^2\mu}{2}\cos\ (4\pi n_2t+f)</math>}}
{{block center|<math>+\frac{ab\lambda}{2}\cos\ \{2\pi(n_1-n_2)t+e\}-\frac{ab\lambda}{2}\cos\ \{2\pi(n_1+n_2)t+e\}</math>}}
{{block center|<math>+\frac{ab\mu}{2}\cos\ \{2\pi(n_1-n_2)t-f\}-\frac{ab\mu}{2}\cos\ \{2\pi(n_1+n_2)t+f\}</math> (35)}}
Thus, accompanying the two original pure tones there are (1) the octave of each; (2) a tone of frequency <math>(n_1-n_2)</math>; (3) a tone of frequency <math>(n_1+n_2)</math>. The second is termed by Helmholtz the ''difference tone'', and the third the ''summation tone''. The amplitudes of

